# Security headers for the Cloudflare Workers static-assets deploy (INF-021).
# Vite's publicDir copy places this at the root of frontend/dist.
#
# Cache-Control is deliberately NOT set here. Cloudflare APPENDS the values of
# every matching rule instead of letting the more specific one win, so a `/*`
# catch-all of `no-store` plus a `/js/*` rule of `immutable` produced
#
#   Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000, immutable
#
# on production, and `no-store` wins per RFC 9111 — the exact opposite of
# INF-020. Reordering does not help; the concatenation follows file order, not
# specificity. INF-022 mandates the fallback that is now in place:
# frontend/worker/index.ts owns Cache-Control and sets it with Headers.set,
# which replaces rather than appends. Do not reintroduce Cache-Control here —
# any value added would be appended to the Worker's and could only weaken it.
#
# The headers below are single-valued and identical for every path, so appending
# cannot corrupt them.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
